---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import DocCallout from "../../components/docs/DocCallout.astro";

const toc = [
  { title: "Layout", href: "#layout", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Migrations", href: "#migrations", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Locks", href: "#locks", depth: 2 },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Storage"
  subtitle="Persistent storage and migrations in packages/nikcli/src/storage."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="layout" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Layout</h2>
    <p>
      Session and tool data are stored as JSON files under <code>Global.Path.data/storage</code>.
      Structured data (users, accounts, workspace state, mobile tokens) is persisted in a SQLite
      database managed by Drizzle ORM with schema migrations run at startup.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="migrations" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Migrations</h2>
    <p>JSON-layer migrations live in <code>Storage.MIGRATIONS</code> and run once per storage version. SQLite schema migrations are handled by Drizzle and applied automatically.</p>
    <DocCallout type="warn" title="Destructive operations">
      <p>Migrations can rewrite or move session data. Always back up before manual edits.</p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="locks" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Locks</h2>
    <p>Reads and writes use file locks to prevent concurrent corruption.</p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
